{
	"id": "promises-only-happy-path",
	"text": "Behold! A checkout function returning a Promise<Order>. Internally, it calls three more async functions. What will happen when we call it? A Promise has but one type parameter: its success value. Here, that's the Order we hope to get. But can checkout fail? And if it does, how will it fail? Unfortunately, Promise is not very forthcoming in this regard.",
	"code": "async function checkout(cartId: string): Promise<Order> {\n  const cart = await getCart(cartId)\n  const payment = await charge(cart)\n  const shipment = await ship(payment)\n  return shipment\n}",
